---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="10 years of Remote ROS Development & Training | RUNTIME Robotics"
  description="Lessons from a decade of remote ROS development, consulting and robotics training."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="page-main">
    <article class="article container narrow">
      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="kicker">ROS · Career</span>
        <h1>10 years of Remote ROS Development & Training, What are the key lessons learned?</h1>
        <p class="blog-date">February 14, 2024</p>
      </header>
      <div class="article-body">
        <p>
          This route is already preserved so existing links can continue to work after the migration.
          The supplied migration script can pull the full WordPress article into this static project before launch.
        </p>
        <p>
          The article looks back at a long career in ROS development and education, including early robotics work,
          remote consulting, technical writing, training, client relationships and the need to keep learning as the
          robotics software ecosystem changes.
        </p>
        <div class="migration-callout">
          <strong>Before going live</strong>
          <p>Run <code>npm run migrate:wp</code> to replace this temporary version with the full exported WordPress post while preserving the original URL.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
